 result←object Draw arg;State;op;fn;operation
 ⍝ Perform a sequence of graphical drawing operations on Pictures, Printers, or any other controls in general
 result←⍬ ⍝ Accumulate any results they might have asked for
 State←InitialState object ⍝ Track current state sequentially throughout the drawing process -- manage it pseudo-globally via a namespace reference

 :For op :In ,¨⊆¨arg ⍝ Loop through the application's entire command sequence in strict order
     fn←Operations ##.Canonize{⍵↓⍨'?'=⊃⍵}⊃op ⍝ Standardize capitalization, since APL+Win allows it to be flexible
     :If fn⊂⍛∊Operations ⍝ For argument validation to keep from calling an unintentional routine
     :AndIf 4=⎕NC fn←fn,⍨'∆'/⍨'?'=⊃⊃op ⍝ Make sure it's been implemented
         ⎕DL 1E¯15 ⍝ This avoids a GUI problem where the object doesn't show up dynamically
         operation←⍎'State ',fn ⍝ Let's implement all the commands as APL operators with the left operand being the modifiable current-state namespace
         result,←fn{(0=≢⍵)∧'∆'=⊃⍺:⎕NULL ⋄ ⍵}object operation 1↓op ⍝ Perform the drawing operation, appending any result values that may be returned (usually just ⍬)
     :Else
         ##.Error'∆WI DRAW ERROR: Invalid draw command "',fn,'"'
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
 :If object._class≡'Printer' ⋄ :AndIf State._dirty∧~object._dirty ⋄ object._dirty←1 ⋄ object ##.∆WS⊂'Dirty' 1 ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Promote printer page dirtiness
 ##.∆EX⍕¨State ⎕VGET('FontObj' '')('IconObj' '')('BrushBmp' '') ⍝ Clean up temporary objects used in this statement

 :If 0=≢result
     result←##.Classes.NoRes ⍝ If we haven't generated any results at all, just return the standard empty result
 :Else
     result←1↓0,result~⎕NULL ⍝ Allow "?" operations to return ⍬ which gets converted to ⎕NULL to signal that a result is always returned
 :EndIf
⍝? Are there any control classes which we need to explicitly prevent drawing upon?
